// src/v4/lens/affected_set.dag
//
// Scope: affected-set lens — given a diff over the dependency graph, derive the MINIMAL subgraph that must re-execute. Canonical authority for incremental execution + CI job selection. scripts/detect-affected-components.sh is the interim BOOTSTRAP BRIDGE; this lens is the structural authority that replaces it (per feedback_no_textual_enforcement_bridges).
// Anchor: THESIS "Free consequences" §205-210 (incremental cross-run execution) + v4-close-interrogation.md §2.5.F affected-set + memory: feedback_no_textual_enforcement_bridges
// Why EARLY (operator 2026-05-15: "something i wanted to get working
//   very early on"): load-bearing for incremental execution AND it is
//   the structural replacement for the shell script currently gating
//   v2/v3/v4 CI selection. Phase 1.5.
//
// GRANULARITY (operator-corrected 2026-05-15): there is ONE real
// granularity — NODE. "File/module-affected" is NOT a separate tier; it
// is node-granularity PROJECTED UP (the set of files containing ≥1
// affected node). Do not model two tiers; model node, project for the
// file/CI view.
//
// WORKED EXAMPLES (the design contract — the T-21 worker fills to satisfy
// these; node-granularity, target-agnostic FACT per the lens discipline):
//
//   Graph (→ = "depends on"; content_hash per node, B1):
//     n_reason  (NamedReason variant set, in std/diagnostic.dag)
//       ← n_diag (Diagnostic { reason }) ← n_emitR (a Rust emit rule)
//       ← n_diag                          ← n_evalD (eval's diag path)
//     n_pure   (a pure helper, no dep on n_reason)
//
//   Ex.1 — add a NamedReason variant. Diff: content_hash(n_reason)
//     changed. forward-closure → { n_reason, n_diag, n_emitR, n_evalD }.
//     ReExecFrontier = those 4. n_pure is SKIPPED — its input hashes are
//     unchanged AND it is pure ⇒ provably same output (THESIS:205-210).
//     File-view (projection): the files containing those 4 nodes.
//
//   Ex.2 — reformat a comment / rename a local (no semantic change).
//     content_hash UNCHANGED (canonical-form + opaque Symbol, K-1/B1 —
//     α-equivalence). Diff empty ⇒ ReExecFrontier = ∅. Nothing re-runs.
//     This is the payoff: cosmetic edits cost zero recompute, BY the hash.
//
//   Ex.3 — change a node whose effect the effect-lens cannot bound.
//     FAIL-CLOSED: the lens cannot PROVE downstream unchanged ⇒ it
//     conservatively INCLUDES the dependents (re-run), never optimistically
//     skips. no-engine: doubt resolves toward more re-execution surfaced,
//     never a fabricated "it's fine."
//
//   Ex.4 — change n_pure only. Frontier = { n_pure } (+ its dependents,
//     none here). n_reason/n_diag/emit/eval all SKIP. Minimal by
//     construction — the forward-closure is exactly the affected cone.
//
// Owns:
//   - affected_set: (Dag, Diff) -> Witness<ReExecFrontier>
//     (NODE granularity — the minimal node set that must re-run;
//     everything else is incrementally skippable because pure +
//     content-hash-unchanged. File/CI view = project the frontier to
//     containing files. fail-closed: unprovable ⇒ included, never skipped)
//   - Diff is STRUCTURAL: a node is "changed" iff its B1 content_hash
//     differs from the prior pin — NOT a textual git diff
//   - composes with compiler/05_eval.dag (skip unchanged pure subgraphs)
//   - composes with workflow/ci.dag (gate/job selection — replaces the
//     interim scripts/detect-affected-components.sh shell bridge)
//
// DOGFOOD REALITY via the frozen v2 seed (operator asked "how fast can we
// dogfood this using v2?" — honest answer, verified 2026-05-15):
//   - v2 HAS a `run` interpreter + emits a structured `dag-artifact.json`
//     (`compile --target dag`). But that artifact is MODULE-level
//     (module/imports/items/span), NOT the Node tree — and v2 is the
//     FROZEN seed: we cannot enrich its emission (A3). So there is NO
//     node-granularity path through v2; node-granularity arrives with the
//     v4 pipeline at T-9 (the typed Dag) — no v2 shortcut exists.
//   - Worse: v2 cleanly compiles ONLY the v4 v2-subset scaffolds, whose
//     artifact has EMPTY imports/items (header-stubs). v2 cannot compile
//     its own src/v2/*.dag or v3 dsl/. So today there is NO corpus with
//     real edges for v2 to compute an affected-set over. A "demo" over
//     edge-empty stubs would be theater = forbidden (no-engine).
//   - Earliest HONEST dogfood = MODULE-granularity over `dag-artifact.json`
//     run by `v2-compiler run` (a hand-authored .dag), once v4 files carry
//     REAL `import`/declarations so the artifact's edges populate. That is
//     gated on (a) real content (T-1/T-3 landing → #3151), and (b) the
//     v2-interpreter pre-flight: can `v2-compiler run` execute the
//     affected-set .dag over the artifact? — verify BEFORE relying on it.
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/witness.dag
//   - lens/effect.dag (effect-independence gates safe skip — Ex.3)
//   - compiler/04_infer.dag: the typed dependency graph (Dag)
//   - std/primitive.dag: Hash (B1 content_hash — the structural Diff)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-21
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.lens.affected_set

